"]},{"name":"gradingScale","subType":"gradingScaleRef","type":"REFERENCE","values":["GRD"]},{"name":"dutchNameShort","type":"STRING","values":["Language Use in the World TEN"]}],"year":{"code":"2026-2027","id":"2261","names":[{"language":"EN","value":"2026-2027"},{"language":"NL","value":"2026-2027"}],"uid":"07254806-916f-4cca-82a0-2e69a4a95e9f"}},"required":true,"values":[{"name":"evaluate","subType":"yesNoReference","type":"REFERENCE","values":["Y"]}],"weighting":1.00}],"capacity":{"optimum":25.00},"code":"5512VEB02Y","credits":{"optimum":5.00},"descriptions":[{"language":"EN","text":"This course builds on the topics discussed in the first semester course Language and Communication and deepens the understanding of the core concepts introduced in that course. The focus of this course is on diversity in the way people think about language use across the globe. What are the (social) norms of language use, what is and is not appropriate behavior, pertaining both to verbal and non-verbal communication? In this course we will concentrate on the similarities and differences found in cross-cultural communication and the linguistic or cultural motives associated with them and we will investigate how patterns of language use are connected to the social-cultural context in which they are observed.\n\nThe course covers the following topics (amongst others): languages and status; language and knowledge; language and politics; language folklore; orality.","type":{"code":"CO","id":"CO","names":[{"language":"EN","value":"Description"},{"language":"NL","value":"Beschrijving"}],"uid":"9b0c3e97-ad09-42d7-a5bb-afdaf6f1877f"}},{"language":"EN","text":"* *Language Use in the World* Syllabus\r\rAdditional readings are announced on Brightspace.","type":{"code":"LI","id":"LI","names":[{"language":"EN","value":"Reading list"},{"language":"NL","value":"Literatuurlijst"}],"uid":"fbd93a9e-ca99-4bcc-807f-39235bb6000b"}},{"language":"EN","text":"### Assessment and weighing\n\n* 2 midterm assignment (40%)\n* Final exam (60%)\n\nTo successfully complete the course, please take note of the following:\n\n* Assignments beyond the deadline are not graded.\n\n\n* The end grade of the course is established by determining the weighted average of both assignments and the final exam.","type":{"code":"TP","id":"TP","names":[{"language":"EN","value":"Assessment method"},{"language":"NL","value":"Toetsing en weging"}],"uid":"687f9ba4-4330-4ab9-8536-be9ebd2c58c5"}},{"language":"EN","text":"Enrolment through MyStudyMap (button in upper right corner) is mandatory. General information about course and exam enrolment is available on the [website](https://www.student.universiteitleiden.nl/en/your-study-programme/courses-and-exams/enrolment/leiden-university)","type":{"code":"ENR","id":"ENR","names":[{"language":"EN","value":"Registration"},{"language":"NL","value":"Inschrijven"}],"uid":"a77a2043-b0a9-450d-b780-1e90a4d3290c"}},{"language":"EN","text":"* Knowledge and understanding of concepts and phenomena related to ethnography of communication.\n* Knowledge of cross-cultural differences and similarities in language use and understanding of the consequences for intercultural communication.\n* Analytic skills to interpret and understand interpersonal communicative interaction.","type":{"code":"LO","id":"LO","names":[{"language":"EN","value":"Course objectives"},{"language":"NL","value":"Leerdoelen"}],"uid":"b54eb210-96e8-490d-aadb-a70571a665d9"}},{"language":"EN","text":"None.","type":{"code":"AR","id":"AR","names":[{"language":"EN","value":"Admission requirements"},{"language":"NL","value":"Toegangseisen"}],"uid":"2c481598-5834-4422-a338-1eb346d6f52c"}},{"language":"EN","text":"For substantive questions, contact the lecturer(s) (listed in the right information bar).  For questions about enrolment, admission, etc., contact the Education Administration Office: [Reuvensplaats](osz-oa-reuvensplaats@hum.leidenuniv.nl)","type":{"code":"CG","id":"CG","names":[{"language":"EN","value":"Contact"},{"language":"NL","value":"Contact"}],"uid":"35f7e88a-830a-4877-b467-86a700954d19"}},{"language":"EN","text":"Lecture","type":{"code":"WV","id":"WV","names":[{"language":"EN","value":"Teaching method"},{"language":"NL","value":"Onderwijsvorm"}],"uid":"26f0e596-e48d-46ff-8c8b-9b9688699943"}},{"language":"EN","text":"The timetables are available through My Timetable (see the button in the upper right corner).","type":{"code":"SC","id":"SC","names":[{"language":"EN","value":"Schedule"},{"language":"NL","value":"Rooster"}],"uid":"939373d2-217d-4dde-9c37-6f6101f1ab75"}},{"language":"EN","text":"### Resit\n\nIf the grade is lower than 5.5, there is only a retake for the final exam.\n\n### Review and feedback \n\nHow and when an exam review takes place will be determined by the examiner. This review will be within 30 days after official publication of exam results.","type":{"code":"RRD","id":"RRD","names":[{"language":"EN","value":"Resit, review & feedback"},{"language":"NL","value":"Herkansing, inzage & nabespreking"}],"uid":"ef7be178-91d7-4f56-a40b-891976f3af1c"}}],"faculty":{"code":"FGW","id":"FGW","names":[{"language":"EN","value":"Humanities"},{"language":"NL","value":"Geesteswetenschappen"}],"uid":"28c8aabb-f896-444f-895c-63ef88ba9307"},"id":"265155","key":108351,"methods":[{"method":{"category":"T","code":"5512VEB02W","contactHours":26.00,"id":"265156","key":125889,"module":{"code":"5512VEB02Y","id":"265155","names":[{"language":"EN","value":"Language Use in the World"},{"language":"NL","value":"Language Use in the World"}],"uid":"d7d72c99-7264-43f8-947c-51510181eed8"},"names":[{"language":"EN","value":"Language Use in the World"},{"language":"NL","value":"Language Use in the World"}],"type":"WGR","typeAbbreviation":"WGR","uid":"937f7415-d83a-4dd9-b50a-831a0f3dcb3d","values":[{"name":"studiegidsnummerY","type":"STRING","values":["5512VEB02Y"]},{"name":"numberOfGroups","values":["1"]},{"name":"examDateFlag","subType":"yesNoReference","type":"REFERENCE","